    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88-a2">

                <pb facs="0146" n="880" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg880"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 107.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Willis to Mr. Hatch.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-07"><hi rendition="#italic">May 7,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    to-day of your note of the 3d instant relating to the termination of the mission
                    of Hon. L. A. Thurston, late minister from your Government to the United States.
                    From it I quote the following: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Referring to our interview on the 30th ultimo, in which you intimated
                            that the President of the United States would he pleased if the Hawaiian
                            minister at Washington should he recalled, for personal reasons, and
                            upon which occasion you read to me a dispatch from the Secretary of
                            State to yourself on this subject, dated February 21, but which had been
                            sent to Japan by mistake, * * *</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>As this passage may lead to a misconception of what occurred, of which I have
                    already informed my Government, you will permit me to recall the fact that the
                    interview referred to by you was limited to the reading of the dispatch of my
                    Government, an explanation of its apparent miscarriage to Hongkong, and the
                    declaration that the regret expressed in the dispatch at the incident was shared
                    by me.</p>
                <p>I will at once transmit your note to my Government for its consideration.</p>
                <p>With assurances, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Albert S. Willis.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
